From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:18:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: release expired reorder frames when the timeout
 is reached

The reorder work is queued mt76_aggr_tid_to_timeo() jiffies after the
first frame is buffered behind a hole, but the expiry check only
releases frames whose timeout has strictly passed. When the work runs on
the expiry jiffy, which is the common case with a low HZ, nothing is
released and the work is re-armed for another full timeout. A lost
frame without a following BAR then stalls the TID for about twice the
intended time (around 200 ms instead of 100 ms for best effort at
HZ=100), which is close to the minimum TCP RTO.

Treat the timeout as expired once it is reached.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 agg-rx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/agg-rx.c b/agg-rx.c
index 3d34caf7..90c8a92c 100644
--- a/agg-rx.c
+++ b/agg-rx.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ mt76_rx_aggr_check_release(struct mt76_rx_tid *tid, struct sk_buff_head *frames)
 
 		nframes--;
 		status = (struct mt76_rx_status *)skb->cb;
-		if (!time_after32(jiffies,
+		if (time_before32(jiffies,
 				  status->reorder_time +
 				  mt76_aggr_tid_to_timeo(tid->num)))
 			continue;
